LumOn - Phase 23.8.X - WorldCell + TraceSceneRegionScheduler

Goal
- [ ] Replace TraceScene’s ad-hoc region queues with a scheduler that provides: dedup by construction, in-place priority updates, backoff/cooldowns for missing chunks, and stable convergence.
- [ ] Introduce a reusable `IWorldCell`/`WorldCell` abstraction for “sub-partitions of world space”, enabling later reuse by LumonScene surface-cache scheduling.

Non-goals (initial)
- [ ] Rewrite LumonScene surface-cache scheduling to fully use `WorldCell` (defer until TraceScene scheduler is proven).
- [ ] Achieve UE5 Lumen parity (this is scheduling + robustness work).


Phase 1 - WorldCell Primitives (Contracts + Types)
- [x] Define `WorldCellKind` enum (TraceSceneRegion, LumonSceneNear/Far, etc.).
- [x] Define `WorldCellKey` (packed `ulong` + kind encoding; allow using `ChunkKey.Packed` for TraceSceneRegion).
- [x] Define `WorldCellPriorityContext` (camera/anchor/window, frame tick, loadedness hints).
- [x] Define `IWorldCell` contract:
  - [x] `Key`, `Kind`, `Priority`, `NextEligibleTick`
  - [x] `CalculatePriority(ctx)` (pure/cheap)
  - [x] versioning fields (`CurrentVersion`, `AppliedVersion`) for staleness detection
- [x] Add base `WorldCell` type with common scheduling fields (heap index, cooldown bookkeeping).
- [x] Add unit tests for key packing/equality + basic priority contract expectations.


Phase 2 - Indexed Priority Queue (No Duplicates, O(logN) Updates)
- [x] Implement `IndexedMaxHeap<TKey>` (or `IndexedPriorityQueue<TKey>`) with:
  - [x] `Upsert(key, priority)`
  - [x] `UpdatePriority(key, priority)`
  - [x] `Remove(key)`
  - [x] `TryPopMax(out key)`
  - [x] O(1) key→heapIndex mapping (stored on entry or in a dictionary)
- [x] Unit tests:
  - [x] insert/pop ordering
  - [x] increase/decrease key updates
  - [x] remove arbitrary key
  - [x] “Upsert does not duplicate”


Phase 3 - TraceSceneRegionCell (WorldCell Specialization)
- [x] Implement `TraceSceneRegionCell : WorldCell` (or `WorldCell` + per-kind payload) with:
  - [x] `ChunkKey` / region coord (chunk units)
  - [x] `MissingStreak`, `LastSeenLoadedTick`, `LastAttemptTick`
  - [x] `CurrentVersion`, `AppliedVersion`, `InFlightVersion`
  - [x] reason flags for priority composition (distance/stale/loaded/missing)
- [x] Define TraceScene priority function terms and constants:
  - [x] distance term (camera or clipmap-anchor based)
  - [x] staleness term (never applied / applied != current)
  - [x] loadedness bonus (recently seen loaded)
  - [x] missing penalty + cooldown gate
- [x] Unit tests for priority ordering across a small synthetic window.


Phase 4 - TraceSceneRegionScheduler (Core Scheduling)
- [x] Create `TraceSceneRegionScheduler` owning:
  - [x] cell dictionary (authoritative entry per region)
  - [x] indexed heap of eligible cells
  - [x] window bounds + incremental window seeding cursor
  - [x] in-flight tracking and completion processing
  - [x] cooldown/backoff computation for `ChunkUnavailable` / snapshot unavailable
- [x] Provide public API (initial sketch):
  - [x] `SetWindow(min,max)`
  - [x] `NotifyChunkDirty(chunkKey, reason)` (optional, internal to TraceScene renderer)
  - [x] `NotifyChunkSeenLoaded(chunkKey)` (optional)
  - [x] `RefreshPriorities(ctx, budget)` (incremental or lazy)
  - [x] `TryDequeueNextEligible(nowTick, out key)` / `DequeueBatch(...)`
  - [x] `OnRequestIssued(key, version)` / `OnRequestCompleted(key, status)`
- [x] Add fairness guarantees:
  - [x] ensure “near window” cells can’t be permanently starved by far cells
  - [x] ensure cooldown-suppressed cells don’t block other work


Phase 5 - Wire Scheduler Into `LumonSceneOccupancyClipmapUpdateRenderer`
- [x] Replace:
  - [x] `pendingRegionsHigh/Low`, `pendingRegionKeys`
  - [x] `maintenanceCursor`, `windowSeedCursor`, `windowSeedTotal`
  - [x] ad-hoc re-enqueue on failure
- [x] Drive scheduling from budgets:
  - [x] keep `ClipmapIssueBudgetMs` / `ClipmapDispatchBudgetMs`
  - [x] use `ClipmapMaxInFlightRegions` as the hard cap
  - [x] keep `ClipmapMaxRegionUploadsPerFrame` / `ClipmapMaxRegionsDispatchedPerFrame` as GPU safety limits
- [x] Ensure TraceScene only reacts to engine `ChunkDirty` via its own subscription (no LumOnModSystem invalidation).
- [x] Add a small “loadedness hint” path using observed chunk events (inside TraceScene renderer).


Phase 6 - Backoff/Cooldown Policy (Convergence Under Missing Chunks)
- [x] Implement exponential backoff for `ChunkUnavailable` with clamp (e.g. up to 5s).
- [x] Add “never retry faster than X ms” to prevent per-frame churn.
- [x] Add “seen loaded recently” override to re-enable quickly when chunk arrives.
- [x] Unit tests:
  - [x] missing chunk does not dominate dequeue results
  - [x] once chunk becomes available, it regains priority and is scheduled promptly


Phase 7 - Metrics + Debugging Hooks
- [x] Add scheduler metrics:
  - [x] eligible heap size
  - [x] suppressed (cooldown) count
  - [x] in-flight count
  - [x] applied count
  - [x] completion breakdown (success/unavailable/canceled/superseded/failed)
  - [x] cooldown skips
- [x] Extend TS overlay string to include scheduler counters (top-k + reason bits).
- [x] Add optional debug “dump scheduler state” log button (top N entries with reason).


Phase 8 - Extend WorldCell For LumonScene (Design-only Follow-up)
- [x] Define `LumonSceneRegionCell : WorldCell` responsibilities (near/far membership + residency/capture/relight summary).
  - Identity: `WorldCellKind.LumonSceneNear|LumonSceneFar` + packed chunk coord (`LumonSceneChunkCoord.ToKey()`).
  - Membership: `Kind` encodes field; `ChunkCoord` is stable even as `chunkSlot` assignment changes.
  - Slot view (near/far window): `ChunkSlot` (uint), `SlotGeneration` (ushort), `LastSeenInSlotTick` (long).
  - Residency summary (per chunk): derived from page table mirror + physical pool mappings.
    - Counts: `ResidentPages`, `NeedsCapture`, `Capturing`, `NeedsRelight`, `Relighting`, `ReadyToSample`.
    - Heat: `FeedbackRequestCount` (or decayed “heat”) from PatchId feedback / usage stamps.
  - Scheduling fields:
    - `CurrentVersion`/`AppliedVersion` represent “content staleness” (e.g. slotGeneration or dirty stamp increments).
    - `NextEligibleTick` for cooldown/backoff when chunk slot is invalid/unloaded or budgets are exhausted.
  - Priority sketch (not implemented): prioritize by (NeedsCapture/NeedsRelight backlog) > (feedback heat / visible demand) > (distance-to-anchor), with penalties for cooldown/missing.

- [x] Define how chunkSlot + generation + atlas residency map into the cell.
  - chunkSlot ownership comes from `LumonSceneFeedbackUpdateRenderer` slot state (`slotOwners` + `chunkToSlot`).
  - `slotGenerations[chunkSlot]` gates validity:
    - if (slotGen mismatch) treat the cell as “not in slot” (unloaded/transitioning) and suppress work.
    - when slot reassigned, that is a “version bump” for the cell (staleness trigger).
  - Virtual page identity is (chunkSlot, virtualPageIndex) via `LumonSceneVirtualPageKeyUtil.Pack(...)`.
  - Atlas residency + readiness is expressed by the page table mirror entry:
    - `virtualToPhysical` / `physicalToVirtual` (CPU maps) + `pageTableMirror` (per-virtual-page flags).
    - `LumonScenePageTableEntryPacking.Flags` drive per-cell work:
      - `NeedsCapture` → capture work
      - `NeedsRelight` → relight work
      - `Capturing`/`Relighting` → in-flight
      - `IsReadyForSampling(...)` → safe to sample for shading/debug.
  - Release/cleanup events (chunk unload / field transition / eviction) should clear mappings + invalidate affected cell summaries.

- [x] Identify which existing LumonScene systems become “cell processors” later:
  - [x] PatchId feedback → capture queue
    - `LumonSceneFeedbackUpdateRenderer` (GPU feedback gather + slot management) and `LumonSceneFeedbackRequestProcessor` (CPU allocation + capture/relight work item creation + page table writes).
  - [x] Relight queue
    - `LumonSceneRelightUpdateRenderer` (currently MRU-based selection; future: consume per-cell relight backlog).
  - [x] Eviction / residency safety rules
    - `LumonSceneChunkResidencyManager` + pool planning/management for page allocation/eviction; releases on chunk unload/field transitions; avoid evicting pages for active slots.


Phase 9 - Desired State (World Partition-Style Cell State Machine)
- [ ] Add a per-cell “desired state” concept (UE5 World Partition inspired):
  - [ ] Define `WorldCellDesiredState` (Unloaded, Loading, Loaded, Unloading, etc.).
  - [ ] Define `WorldCellActualState` (current lifecycle state) if needed.
  - [ ] Define allowed transitions + invariants (no illegal skips, cancellation rules).
- [ ] Extend `IWorldCell`/`WorldCell`:
  - [ ] `DesiredState` property
  - [ ] `ActualState` property (optional but recommended for debugging)
  - [ ] `CalculateDesiredState(ctx)` (pure/cheap, similar to `CalculatePriority`)
- [ ] Add a `WorldCellStateTransitionContext` (loadedness hints, resource budgets, distance thresholds).
- [ ] Add a generic `WorldCellStateMachine` helper:
  - [ ] transition evaluator (Desired→Actual)
  - [ ] per-state actions interface (enqueue load, enqueue unload, cancel in-flight, etc.)
  - [ ] backoff/cooldown integration for failed transitions
- [ ] Integrate desired-state with the scheduler:
  - [ ] scheduler should only consider cells eligible for “work” when DesiredState requires it
  - [ ] avoid thrash by adding hysteresis (e.g., hold Loaded until outside radius for N frames)
- [ ] Tests:
  - [ ] deterministic desired-state decisions for a synthetic camera path
  - [ ] transition ordering correctness (no illegal transitions)
  - [ ] thrash prevention (hysteresis works)
